WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:02.821
Coding standards are agreements about how software should

00:00:02.844 --> 00:00:03.994
be written and maintained.

00:00:04.435 --> 00:00:07.512
You do not have to read every line of code to benefit from

00:00:07.558 --> 00:00:07.837
them.

00:00:08.278 --> 00:00:11.865
Ask whether a module has a clear responsibility, whether

00:00:11.958 --> 00:00:15.186
names explain intent, whether inputs are checked at

00:00:15.244 --> 00:00:17.891
boundaries, and whether the next person can find the

00:00:17.914 --> 00:00:18.460
behavior.

00:00:19.157 --> 00:00:21.734
Standards should help the agent create software that can

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.787
be understood and changed without relying on the original

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:25.658
author's memory.
